## What this bundle guarantees

| Level | Meaning | Status for this bundle |
| --- | --- | --- |
| R1 Prediction parity | Reloading `model/model.joblib` and predicting on `parity/parity_input.csv` reproduces `parity/parity_expected.json`: class labels exactly, probabilities or values within 1e-9. | **Verified at export** ({{ parity_rows }} synthetic rows, max abs diff {{ parity_diff }}). Guaranteed with the pinned `requirements.txt` on Linux x86-64 or macOS arm64 with Python 3.11. |
| R2 Retraining parity | `python pipeline.py train` on the same development rows rebuilds a model whose parity predictions match within 1e-6 (probabilities). | Target, tested on fixture datasets with deterministic settings. Not guaranteed across CPU architectures, thread counts or library versions. |
| R3 CV parity | Re-running TabPilot reproduces cross-validation means within ±0.5% relative. | Target in trial-count tuning mode on the same environment. Runs limited by wall-clock time can complete different numbers of trials and differ. |

Results can also vary with library versions, hardware, BLAS threading and algorithms that are
not deterministic.

## Commands

Run these from the bundle directory after `pip install -r requirements.txt` (Python 3.11):

```
python pipeline.py verify
python pipeline.py predict --model model/model.joblib --input new.csv --out predictions.csv
python pipeline.py train --data dev.csv --out retrained.joblib
python pipeline.py train --data original_file.csv --resplit --out retrained.joblib
```

`pipeline.py` and `model.joblib` load the bundled `tabpilot_runtime/` package (it sits next to
`pipeline.py`); the `tabpilot` application itself is not needed. `--resplit` drops rows with a
missing target and selects the recorded development row positions, which recreates the original
split only for the same file in the same row order. TabPilot's own file repairs (encoding
detection, decimal commas, malformed lines) are not repeated by `pipeline.py`; supply a clean
CSV.

